IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sg-definitions`
IMPORT `sg-interpretation`
IMPORT `sgo-penalties`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), Part 12 Division 2: the offences of ss 401 to 406 (false and misleading statements, false statements or reports,
-- dividends payable from profits only, obtaining payments by false promise, carrying on business without registering and improper use of words in a name,
-- frauds by officers). The general penalty (s 407), the default penalty (s 408) and the "officer who is in default" are in sgo-penalties.l4. Part agent sgo.
--
-- Every offence is a function over the facts that answers JUST TRUE where every element holds and NOTHING where an element fails: the section says
-- "shall be guilty" of the person who does the act and says nothing of the person who does not (fork register, split site type (i)). The only JUST FALSE of an offence
-- is an "unless" that the text writes into the offence itself (s 405(1) "unless at that time the business was duly incorporated under this Act").
-- Each offence has a penalty function that returns a `Penalty` (sg-core.l4) for the person guilty of it.

DECLARE `s 402(1) recipient of the statement or report` IS ONE OF
    `s 402(1)(a) a director, auditor, member, debenture holder or trustee for debenture holders of the corporation`
    `s 402(1)(b) an auditor of the holding company of a corporation that is a subsidiary`
    `s 402(1) someone else`

DECLARE `s 401 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 401(1) advertise, circulate or publish a misleading statement of the amount of capital`
    `s 401(2) wilfully make or authorise a false or misleading statement in a document required by or for the purposes of this Act`
    `s 401(2A) lodge a document with the Registrar knowing it to be false or misleading in a material respect`

DECLARE `s 402 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 402(1) make or furnish, with intent to deceive, a false or misleading statement or report relating to the affairs of the corporation`

DECLARE `s 403 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 403(1) pay a dividend except out of profits`
    `s 403(2) wilfully pay or permit to be paid a dividend in contravention of section 403`

DECLARE `s 404 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 404(3) by deceitful means or false promise and with intent to defraud, cause money to be paid or a chattel or marketable security to be delivered`

DECLARE `s 405 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 405(1) use a name ending in the word Limited or Berhad, or hold out that the business is incorporated under this Act, when it is not`
    `s 405(2) use the word Private or Sendirian in the name of a company that does not fulfil the requirements for private companies`
    `s 405(3) hold out that the business is registered as a foreign company when it is not`

DECLARE `s 406 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 406 while an officer of a company, defraud the company's creditors or induce credit by fraud`

§ `Section 401: false and misleading statements`

§§ `Section 401(1): a misleading statement of the amount of capital`

-- "advertises, circulates or publishes any statement of the amount of its capital which is misleading, or in which the amount of capital or subscribed capital is stated
-- but the amount of paid-up capital or the amount of any charge on uncalled capital is not stated as prominently as the amount of subscribed capital is stated".
-- src:27848 | 401.—(1) Every corporation which advertises, circulates or
-- src:27849 | publishes any statement of the amount of its capital which is
-- src:27850 | misleading, or in which the amount of capital or subscribed capital is
-- src:27851 | stated but the amount of paid‑up capital or the amount of any charge
-- src:27852 | on uncalled capital is not stated as prominently as the amount of
-- src:27853 | subscribed capital is stated, and every officer of the corporation who
-- src:27854 | knowingly authorises, directs or consents to such advertising,
-- src:27855 | circulation or publication shall be guilty of an offence.
@ref s 401(1) (src:27848-27855)
GIVEN `the corporation advertises, circulates or publishes a statement of the amount of its capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement is misleading` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of capital or subscribed capital is stated in the statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of paid-up capital or the amount of any charge on uncalled capital is not stated as prominently as the amount of subscribed capital is stated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 401(1) the corporation is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF    `the corporation advertises, circulates or publishes a statement of the amount of its capital`
       AND (`the statement is misleading` OR (`the amount of capital or subscribed capital is stated in the statement` AND `the amount of paid-up capital or the amount of any charge on uncalled capital is not stated as prominently as the amount of subscribed capital is stated`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "Every corporation which advertises, circulates or publishes any statement ... shall be guilty of an offence" says nothing of a corporation for which an element fails; unmet element of an offence (split site type (i))

@ref s 401(1) (src:27848-27855)
GIVEN `the corporation advertises, circulates or publishes a statement of the amount of its capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement is misleading` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of capital or subscribed capital is stated in the statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of paid-up capital or the amount of any charge on uncalled capital is not stated as prominently as the amount of subscribed capital is stated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer of the corporation knowingly authorises, directs or consents to such advertising, circulation or publication` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 401(1) the officer of the corporation is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF    `the officer of the corporation knowingly authorises, directs or consents to such advertising, circulation or publication`
       AND `the corporation advertises, circulates or publishes a statement of the amount of its capital`
       AND (`the statement is misleading` OR (`the amount of capital or subscribed capital is stated in the statement` AND `the amount of paid-up capital or the amount of any charge on uncalled capital is not stated as prominently as the amount of subscribed capital is stated`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "every officer of the corporation who knowingly authorises, directs or consents to such advertising, circulation or publication shall be guilty of an offence"; unmet element of an offence (split site type (i))

-- The subsection states no penalty, so s 407(2) fixes it: "to a fine not exceeding $1,000" (finding in NOTES.md).
@ref s 401(1) (src:27848-27855)
GIVEN `the person is guilty of an offence under section 401(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 401(1) the highest penalty on conviction` MEANS
    `s 407(2) the highest penalty or punishment on conviction` `the person is guilty of an offence under section 401(1)` NOTHING

@ref s 401(1) (src:27848-27855)
GIVEN `the name of the corporation` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 401 act`
`s 401(1) a corporation must not advertise a misleading statement of its capital` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the corporation`
    SHANT `s 401(1) advertise, circulate or publish a misleading statement of the amount of capital`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the corporation` BECAUSE "the corporation advertised, circulated or published a misleading statement of the amount of its capital"

§§ `Section 401(2), (2A) and (3): a false or misleading statement in a document`

-- src:27885 | (3) For the purposes of subsection (2), where a person at a meeting
-- src:27886 | votes in favour of the making of a statement mentioned in that
-- src:27887 | subsection the person is deemed to have authorised the making of that
-- src:27888 | statement.
@ref s 401(3) (src:27885-27888)
GIVEN `the person votes at a meeting in favour of the making of the statement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 401(3) the person is deemed to have authorised the making of the statement` MEANS
    IF `the person votes at a meeting in favour of the making of the statement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where a person at a meeting votes in favour of the making of a statement mentioned in that subsection the person is deemed to have authorised the making of that statement"; the subsection says nothing of authorising in another way

-- src:27857 | (2) Every person who in any return, report, certificate, balance
-- src:27858 | sheet, financial statements or other document required by or for the
-- src:27859 | purposes of this Act wilfully makes or authorises the making of a
-- src:27860 | statement false or misleading in any material particular knowing it to
-- src:27861 | be false or misleading or wilfully omits or authorises the omission of
-- src:27862 | any matter or thing without which the document is misleading in a
-- src:27863 | material respect shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on
-- src:27864 | conviction to a fine not exceeding $50,000 or to imprisonment for a
-- src:27865 | term not exceeding 2 years or to both.
@ref s 401(2) (src:27857-27865)
GIVEN `the statement is in a return, report, certificate, balance sheet, financial statements or other document required by or for the purposes of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement is false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows the statement to be false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person wilfully makes the statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person wilfully authorises the making of the statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person votes at a meeting in favour of the making of the statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person wilfully omits, or authorises the omission of, a matter or thing without which the document is misleading in a material respect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 401(2) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF    `the statement is in a return, report, certificate, balance sheet, financial statements or other document required by or for the purposes of this Act`
       AND (   (    `the statement is false or misleading in a material particular`
                AND `the person knows the statement to be false or misleading`
                AND (   `the person wilfully makes the statement`
                     OR `the person wilfully authorises the making of the statement`
                     OR `s 401(3) the person is deemed to have authorised the making of the statement` `the person votes at a meeting in favour of the making of the statement` EQUALS JUST TRUE))
            OR `the person wilfully omits, or authorises the omission of, a matter or thing without which the document is misleading in a material respect`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "Every person who in any return, report ... wilfully makes or authorises the making of a statement false or misleading ... shall be guilty of an offence" says nothing of a person for whom an element fails; unmet element of an offence (split site type (i))

@ref s 401(2) (src:27857-27865)
GIVEN `the person is guilty of an offence under section 401(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 401(2) the highest penalty on conviction` MEANS
    IF `the person is guilty of an offence under section 401(2)`
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 50000, 24, TRUE, FALSE)   -- a fine not exceeding $50,000 or imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or to both
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the penalty is that of a person guilty of the offence

@ref s 401(2) (src:27857-27865)
GIVEN `the name of the person` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 401 act`
`s 401(2) a person must not wilfully make or authorise a false or misleading statement in a required document` MEANS
    PARTY Individual `the name of the person`
    SHANT `s 401(2) wilfully make or authorise a false or misleading statement in a document required by or for the purposes of this Act`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Individual `the name of the person` BECAUSE "the person wilfully made or authorised a false or misleading statement in a document required by or for the purposes of this Act"

-- src:27869 | (2A) Any person who, for any purpose under this Act —
-- src:27871 | (a) lodges or files with or submits to the Registrar any
-- src:27872 | document; or
-- src:27874 | (b) authorises another person to lodge or file with or submit to
-- src:27875 | the Registrar any document,
-- src:27880 | knowing that document to be false or misleading in a material respect,
-- src:27881 | shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine
-- src:27882 | not exceeding $50,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:27883 | 2 years or to both.
@ref s 401(2A) (src:27869-27883)
GIVEN `the person lodges or files with or submits to the Registrar a document for a purpose under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person authorises another person to lodge or file with or submit to the Registrar a document for a purpose under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows the document to be false or misleading in a material respect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 401(2A) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF (`the person lodges or files with or submits to the Registrar a document for a purpose under this Act` OR `the person authorises another person to lodge or file with or submit to the Registrar a document for a purpose under this Act`) AND `the person knows the document to be false or misleading in a material respect`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "Any person who, for any purpose under this Act, (a) lodges or files ...; or (b) authorises another person ..., knowing that document to be false or misleading in a material respect, shall be guilty of an offence"; unmet element of an offence (split site type (i))

@ref s 401(2A) (src:27869-27883)
GIVEN `the person is guilty of an offence under section 401(2A)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 401(2A) the highest penalty on conviction` MEANS
    IF `the person is guilty of an offence under section 401(2A)`
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 50000, 24, TRUE, FALSE)   -- a fine not exceeding $50,000 or imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or to both
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the penalty is that of a person guilty of the offence

@ref s 401(2A) (src:27869-27883)
GIVEN `the name of the person` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 401 act`
`s 401(2A) a person must not lodge a document with the Registrar knowing it to be false or misleading` MEANS
    PARTY Individual `the name of the person`
    SHANT `s 401(2A) lodge a document with the Registrar knowing it to be false or misleading in a material respect`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Individual `the name of the person` BECAUSE "the person lodged a document with the Registrar knowing it to be false or misleading in a material respect"

§ `Section 402: false statements or reports`

-- The seam the keel asks of this section (PLAN.md section 4, table A, s 4(8)): "the reference is in section 8A, 8C, 8D, 216, Part 9 or section 402".
-- The words "relating to the affairs of the corporation" in s 402(1) are such a reference.
-- src:27892 | 402.—(1) An officer of a corporation who, with intent to deceive,
-- src:27893 | makes or furnishes, or knowingly and wilfully authorises or permits
-- src:27894 | the making or furnishing of, any false or misleading statement or
-- src:27895 | report to —
-- src:27897 | (a) a director, auditor, member, debenture holder or trustee for
-- src:27898 | debenture holders of the corporation; or
-- src:27900 | (b) in the case of a corporation that is a subsidiary, an auditor
-- src:27901 | of the holding company,
-- src:27903 | relating to the affairs of the corporation, shall be guilty of an offence
-- src:27904 | and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $10,000 or to
-- src:27905 | imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or to both.
@ref s 402(1) (src:27892-27905)
GIVEN `the reference is the words "relating to the affairs of the corporation" in section 402(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 402(1) the reference is in section 402` MEANS
    `the reference is the words "relating to the affairs of the corporation" in section 402(1)`

-- src:27907 | (2) In subsection (1), “officer” includes a person who at any time
-- src:27908 | has been an officer of the corporation.
@ref s 402(2) (src:27907-27908)
GIVEN `the person at any time has been an officer of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 402(2) the person is within the word officer in subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF `the person at any time has been an officer of the corporation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "In subsection (1), \"officer\" includes a person who at any time has been an officer of the corporation"

-- src:27892 | 402.—(1) An officer of a corporation who, with intent to deceive,
-- src:27893 | makes or furnishes, or knowingly and wilfully authorises or permits
-- src:27894 | the making or furnishing of, any false or misleading statement or
-- src:27895 | report to —
-- src:27897 | (a) a director, auditor, member, debenture holder or trustee for
-- src:27898 | debenture holders of the corporation; or
-- src:27900 | (b) in the case of a corporation that is a subsidiary, an auditor
-- src:27901 | of the holding company,
-- src:27903 | relating to the affairs of the corporation, shall be guilty of an offence
-- src:27904 | and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $10,000 or to
-- src:27905 | imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or to both.
@ref s 402(1) (src:27892-27905)
GIVEN matter IS A `s 4(8) matter`
      `the corporation is a trustee and is not a trustee corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act or thing was done at a time when a receiver, or a receiver and manager, was in possession of or had control over property of the corporation, the corporation was under judicial management, a compromise or an arrangement between the corporation and another person was being administered, or the corporation was being wound up` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation has issued interests` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 402(1) the statement or report relates to the affairs of the corporation` MEANS
    `s 4(8) a reference to the affairs of a corporation covers the matter` TRUE FALSE matter `the corporation is a trustee and is not a trustee corporation` `the act or thing was done at a time when a receiver, or a receiver and manager, was in possession of or had control over property of the corporation, the corporation was under judicial management, a compromise or an arrangement between the corporation and another person was being administered, or the corporation was being wound up` `the corporation has issued interests`

@ref s 402(1) (src:27892-27905)
GIVEN position IS A `s 4(1) "officer" what the person is`
      `the person at any time has been an officer of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person makes or furnishes the statement or report with intent to deceive` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knowingly and wilfully authorises or permits the making or furnishing of the statement or report` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement or report is false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN
      recipient IS A `s 402(1) recipient of the statement or report`
      `the corporation is a subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement or report relates to the affairs of the corporation as section 4(8) construes the words` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 402(1) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF    (`s 4(1) "officer" the person is an officer of the corporation` position EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 402(2) the person is within the word officer in subsection (1)` `the person at any time has been an officer of the corporation` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
       AND `the statement or report is false or misleading`
       AND (`the person makes or furnishes the statement or report with intent to deceive` OR `the person knowingly and wilfully authorises or permits the making or furnishing of the statement or report`)
       AND `the statement or report relates to the affairs of the corporation as section 4(8) construes the words`
       AND (CONSIDER recipient
            WHEN `s 402(1)(a) a director, auditor, member, debenture holder or trustee for debenture holders of the corporation` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `s 402(1)(b) an auditor of the holding company of a corporation that is a subsidiary` THEN `the corporation is a subsidiary`
            OTHERWISE FALSE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "An officer of a corporation who, with intent to deceive, makes or furnishes ... any false or misleading statement or report to (a) ...; or (b) ... relating to the affairs of the corporation, shall be guilty of an offence" says nothing of a person for whom an element fails; unmet element of an offence (split site type (i))

@ref s 402(1) (src:27892-27905)
GIVEN `the person is guilty of an offence under section 402(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 402(1) the highest penalty on conviction` MEANS
    IF `the person is guilty of an offence under section 402(1)`
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 10000, 24, TRUE, FALSE)   -- a fine not exceeding $10,000 or imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or to both
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the penalty is that of a person guilty of the offence

@ref s 402(1) (src:27892-27905)
GIVEN `the name of the officer` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 402 act`
`s 402(1) an officer must not make a false or misleading statement or report to a director, auditor or member with intent to deceive` MEANS
    PARTY Officer `the name of the officer`
    SHANT `s 402(1) make or furnish, with intent to deceive, a false or misleading statement or report relating to the affairs of the corporation`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Officer `the name of the officer` BECAUSE "the officer made or furnished, with intent to deceive, a false or misleading statement or report relating to the affairs of the corporation"

§ `Section 403: dividends payable from profits only`

-- src:27912 | 403.—(1) No dividend is payable to the share‑holders of any
-- src:27913 | company except out of profits.
@ref s 403(1) (src:27912-27913)
GIVEN `the dividend is payable to the share-holders of a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the dividend is paid out of profits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 403(1) the dividend is barred because it is not payable out of profits` MEANS
    IF NOT `the dividend is payable to the share-holders of a company`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No dividend is payable to the share-holders of any company"
    ELSE (IF `the dividend is paid out of profits`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except out of profits" (an "except" once met: this subsection does not bar a dividend paid out of profits; fork F-403-1)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

@ref s 403(1) (src:27912-27913)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 403 act`
`s 403(1) a company must not pay a dividend except out of profits` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    SHANT `s 403(1) pay a dividend except out of profits`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company paid a dividend otherwise than out of profits"

-- src:27915 | (1A) Subject to subsection (1B), any profits of a company applied
-- src:27916 | towards the purchase or acquisition of its own shares in accordance
-- src:27917 | with sections 76B to 76G are not payable as dividends to the
-- src:27918 | shareholders of the company.
@ref s 403(1A) (src:27915-27918)
GIVEN `the profits of the company are applied towards the purchase or acquisition of its own shares in accordance with sections 76B to 76G` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection (1B) applies to the amount` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 403(1A) the profits are barred from being paid as dividends to the shareholders` MEANS
    IF NOT `the profits of the company are applied towards the purchase or acquisition of its own shares in accordance with sections 76B to 76G`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any profits of a company applied towards the purchase or acquisition of its own shares in accordance with sections 76B to 76G"
    ELSE (IF `subsection (1B) applies to the amount`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to subsection (1B)"; where (1B) applies the bar does not
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- src:27920 | (1B) Subsection (1A) does not apply to any part of the proceeds
-- src:27921 | received by the company as consideration for the sale or disposal of
-- src:27922 | treasury shares which the company has applied towards the profits of
-- src:27923 | the company.
@ref s 403(1B) (src:27920-27923)
GIVEN `the amount is part of the proceeds received by the company as consideration for the sale or disposal of treasury shares which the company has applied towards the profits of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 403(1B) subsection (1A) does not apply to the amount` MEANS
    IF `the amount is part of the proceeds received by the company as consideration for the sale or disposal of treasury shares which the company has applied towards the profits of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsection (1A) does not apply to any part of the proceeds received by the company as consideration for the sale or disposal of treasury shares which the company has applied towards the profits of the company"

-- src:27928 | (1C) Any gains derived by the company from the sale or disposal of
-- src:27929 | treasury shares are not payable as dividends to the shareholders of the
-- src:27930 | company.
@ref s 403(1C) (src:27928-27930)
GIVEN `the gains are derived by the company from the sale or disposal of treasury shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 403(1C) the gains are barred from being paid as dividends to the shareholders` MEANS
    IF `the gains are derived by the company from the sale or disposal of treasury shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any gains derived by the company from the sale or disposal of treasury shares"

-- (2): "Every director or chief executive officer of a company who wilfully pays or permits to be paid any dividend in contravention of this section".
-- "director" and "chief executive officer" are s 4(1) terms: the keel's functions decide them from the facts below.
-- src:27932 | (2) Every director or chief executive officer of a company who
-- src:27933 | wilfully pays or permits to be paid any dividend in contravention of
-- src:27934 | this section —
-- src:27936 | (a) shall, without prejudice to any other liability, be guilty of
-- src:27937 | an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:27938 | exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not
-- src:27939 | exceeding 12 months; and
@ref s 403(2) (src:27932-27939)
GIVEN `the person occupies the position of director of the corporation, by whatever name called` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors or the majority of the directors of the corporation are accustomed to act in accordance with the person's directions or instructions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors or the majority of the directors act on advice the person gives in a professional capacity, and that is the only reason they follow the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an alternate or substitute director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is in direct employment of, or acting for or by arrangement with, the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is principally responsible for the management and conduct of the business of the company, or part of the business of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person wilfully pays or permits to be paid a dividend` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the dividend is in contravention of section 403` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 403(2) the person is a director or chief executive officer who wilfully pays or permits to be paid a dividend in contravention of section 403` MEANS
    IF    (   `s 4(1) "director" the person is within the word director` `the person occupies the position of director of the corporation, by whatever name called` `the directors or the majority of the directors of the corporation are accustomed to act in accordance with the person's directions or instructions` `the directors or the majority of the directors act on advice the person gives in a professional capacity, and that is the only reason they follow the person` `the person is an alternate or substitute director` EQUALS JUST TRUE
          OR `s 4(1) "chief executive officer" the person is a chief executive officer of the company` `the person is in direct employment of, or acting for or by arrangement with, the company` `the person is principally responsible for the management and conduct of the business of the company, or part of the business of the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
       AND `the person wilfully pays or permits to be paid a dividend`
       AND `the dividend is in contravention of section 403`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "Every director or chief executive officer of a company who wilfully pays or permits to be paid any dividend in contravention of this section" says nothing of a person for whom an element fails; unmet element of an offence (split site type (i))

@ref s 403(2) (src:27932-27939)
GIVEN `the person is a director or chief executive officer who wilfully pays or permits to be paid a dividend in contravention of section 403` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 403(2)(a) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the person is a director or chief executive officer who wilfully pays or permits to be paid a dividend in contravention of section 403`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): unmet element of an offence (split site type (i))

@ref s 403(2) (src:27932-27939)
GIVEN `the person is guilty of an offence under section 403(2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 403(2)(a) the highest penalty on conviction` MEANS
    IF `the person is guilty of an offence under section 403(2)(a)`
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 5000, 12, FALSE, FALSE)   -- a fine not exceeding $5,000 or imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months (not both: "or", not "or to both")
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the penalty is that of a person guilty of the offence

@ref s 403(2) (src:27932-27939)
GIVEN `the name of the director` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 403 act`
`s 403(2) a director or chief executive officer must not wilfully pay or permit a dividend in contravention of section 403` MEANS
    PARTY Director `the name of the director`
    SHANT `s 403(2) wilfully pay or permit to be paid a dividend in contravention of section 403`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Director `the name of the director` BECAUSE "the director wilfully paid or permitted to be paid a dividend in contravention of section 403"

-- (b): "shall also be liable to the creditors of the company for the amount of the debts due by the company to them respectively to the extent by which the dividends so paid have exceeded the profits".
-- The creditors, or the liquidator suing on their behalf, may recover it. The amount is the smaller of the debts due and the excess of the dividends over the profits.
-- src:27941 | (b) shall also be liable to the creditors of the company for the
-- src:27942 | amount of the debts due by the company to them
-- src:27943 | respectively to the extent by which the dividends so paid
-- src:27944 | have exceeded the profits and such amount may be
-- src:27945 | recovered by the creditors or the liquidator suing on
-- src:27946 | behalf of the creditors.
@ref s 403(2)(b) (src:27941-27946)
GIVEN `the person is a director or chief executive officer who wilfully pays or permits to be paid a dividend in contravention of section 403` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the debts due by the company to the creditors, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the dividends so paid, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the profits of the company, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 403(2)(b) the amount the person is liable to the creditors for` MEANS
    IF `the person is a director or chief executive officer who wilfully pays or permits to be paid a dividend in contravention of section 403`
    THEN JUST (IF `the dividends so paid, in Singapore dollars` MINUS `the profits of the company, in Singapore dollars` GREATER THAN 0
               THEN min `the debts due by the company to the creditors, in Singapore dollars` (`the dividends so paid, in Singapore dollars` MINUS `the profits of the company, in Singapore dollars`)
               ELSE 0)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall also be liable to the creditors of the company"; the liability is that of the director or chief executive officer described in the opening words

-- src:27950 | (3) If the whole amount is recovered from one director or chief
-- src:27951 | executive officer, he or she may recover contribution against any
-- src:27952 | other person liable who has directed or consented to such payment.
@ref s 403(3) (src:27950-27952)
GIVEN `the whole amount is recovered from one director or chief executive officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person is liable and has directed or consented to the payment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 403(3) the director or chief executive officer may recover contribution against the other person` MEANS
    IF `the whole amount is recovered from one director or chief executive officer` AND `the other person is liable and has directed or consented to the payment`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the whole amount is recovered from one director or chief executive officer, he or she may recover contribution against any other person liable who has directed or consented to such payment" is an "if" gate on a grant (grant rule of 2026-11-12, limit 1)

-- src:27956 | (4) No liability by this section imposed on any person extends or
-- src:27957 | passes, on the death of such person to the person’s executors or
-- src:27958 | administrators nor is the estate of any such person after the person’s
-- src:27959 | death liable under this section.
@ref s 403(4) (src:27956-27959)
GIVEN `the person has died` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 403(4) the liability extends or passes to the person's executors or administrators or is a liability of the person's estate` MEANS
    IF `the person has died`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No liability by this section imposed on any person extends or passes, on the death of such person to the person's executors or administrators nor is the estate of any such person after the person's death liable under this section"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on the death of such person"

-- src:27961 | (5) In this section, “dividend” includes bonus and payment by way
-- src:27962 | of bonus.
@ref s 403(5) (src:27961-27962)
GIVEN `the payment is a bonus or a payment by way of bonus` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 403(5) the payment is within the word dividend` MEANS
    IF `the payment is a bonus or a payment by way of bonus`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "\"dividend\" includes bonus and payment by way of bonus"

§ `Section 404: obtaining payment by false promise`

-- src:27974 | (3) Whoever, being an officer or agent of any corporation, by any
-- src:27975 | deceitful means or false promise and with intent to defraud, causes or
-- src:27976 | procures any money to be paid or any chattel or marketable security
-- src:27977 | to be delivered to that corporation or to himself, herself or any other
-- src:27978 | person for the use or benefit or on account of that corporation shall be
-- src:27979 | guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:27980 | exceeding $15,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:27981 | 5 years or to both.
@ref s 404(3) (src:27974-27981)
GIVEN `the person is an officer or agent of a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person uses deceitful means or a false promise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts with intent to defraud` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person causes or procures money to be paid, or a chattel or marketable security to be delivered, to the corporation or to himself, herself or any other person for the use or benefit or on account of that corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 404(3) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF    `the person is an officer or agent of a corporation`
       AND `the person uses deceitful means or a false promise`
       AND `the person acts with intent to defraud`
       AND `the person causes or procures money to be paid, or a chattel or marketable security to be delivered, to the corporation or to himself, herself or any other person for the use or benefit or on account of that corporation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "Whoever, being an officer or agent of any corporation, by any deceitful means or false promise and with intent to defraud, causes or procures any money to be paid ... shall be guilty of an offence" says nothing of a person for whom an element fails; unmet element of an offence (split site type (i))

@ref s 404(3) (src:27974-27981)
GIVEN `the person is guilty of an offence under section 404(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 404(3) the highest penalty on conviction` MEANS
    IF `the person is guilty of an offence under section 404(3)`
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 15000, 60, TRUE, FALSE)   -- a fine not exceeding $15,000 or imprisonment for a term not exceeding 5 years or to both
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the penalty is that of a person guilty of the offence

@ref s 404(3) (src:27974-27981)
GIVEN `the name of the person` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 404 act`
`s 404(3) an officer or agent must not cause money to be paid to a corporation by deceitful means or false promise` MEANS
    PARTY Individual `the name of the person`
    SHANT `s 404(3) by deceitful means or false promise and with intent to defraud, cause money to be paid or a chattel or marketable security to be delivered`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Individual `the name of the person` BECAUSE "the person, an officer or agent of a corporation, by deceitful means or false promise and with intent to defraud, caused money to be paid or a chattel or marketable security to be delivered"

-- (4): the opinion of "any registered or public accountant" as to the financial position of a company is admissible in evidence on the trial of a charge under this section.
-- src:27985 | (4) Upon the trial of a charge of an offence under this section, the
-- src:27986 | opinion of any registered or public accountant as to the financial
-- src:27987 | position of any company at any time or during any period in respect of
-- src:27988 | which he or she has made an audit or examination of the affairs of the
-- src:27989 | company according to recognised audit practice is admissible either
-- src:27990 | for the prosecution or for the defence as evidence of the financial
-- src:27991 | position of the company at that time or during that period,
-- src:27992 | notwithstanding that the opinion is based in whole or in part on
-- src:27993 | book‑entries, documents or vouchers or on written or verbal
-- src:27994 | statements by other persons.
@ref s 404(4) (src:27985-27994)
GIVEN `the trial is of a charge of an offence under section 404` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a registered accountant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is registered, or deemed to be registered, under the Accountants Act 2004 as a public accountant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the opinion is as to the financial position of a company at a time or during a period in respect of which the accountant has made an audit or examination of the affairs of the company according to recognised audit practice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 404(4) the accountant's opinion is admissible as evidence of the financial position of the company` MEANS
    IF    `the trial is of a charge of an offence under section 404`
       AND (`the person is a registered accountant` OR `s 4(1) "public accountant" the person is a public accountant` `the person is registered, or deemed to be registered, under the Accountants Act 2004 as a public accountant` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
       AND `the opinion is as to the financial position of a company at a time or during a period in respect of which the accountant has made an audit or examination of the affairs of the company according to recognised audit practice`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- "either for the prosecution or for the defence", and "notwithstanding that the opinion is based in whole or in part on book-entries, documents or vouchers or on written or verbal statements by other persons": neither is asked
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the opinion of any registered or public accountant as to the financial position of any company ... is admissible"; the subsection says nothing of another opinion

§ `Section 405: carrying on business without registering a corporation, and improper use of words`

-- src:28000 | 405.—(1) If any person —
-- src:28002 | (a) other than a foreign company, uses any name or title or
-- src:28003 | trades or carries on business under any name or title which
-- src:28004 | “Limited” or “Berhad” or any abbreviation, imitation or
-- src:28005 | translation of any of those words is the final word; or
-- src:28007 | (b) in any way holds out that the business is incorporated
-- src:28008 | under this Act,
-- src:28010 | that person shall, unless at that time the business was duly
-- src:28016 | liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $10,000 or to
-- src:28017 | imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or to both.
@ref s 405(1) (src:28000-28017)
GIVEN `the person is a foreign company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person uses a name or title, or trades or carries on business under a name or title, of which "Limited" or "Berhad" or any abbreviation, imitation or translation of those words is the final word` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person in any way holds out that the business is incorporated under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at that time the business was duly incorporated under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 405(1) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF NOT (((NOT `the person is a foreign company`) AND `the person uses a name or title, or trades or carries on business under a name or title, of which "Limited" or "Berhad" or any abbreviation, imitation or translation of those words is the final word`) OR `the person in any way holds out that the business is incorporated under this Act`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "If any person (a) other than a foreign company, uses any name or title ...; or (b) in any way holds out that the business is incorporated under this Act" says nothing of a person for whom no limb holds; unmet element of an offence (split site type (i))
    ELSE (IF `at that time the business was duly incorporated under this Act`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that person shall, unless at that time the business was duly incorporated under this Act, be guilty of an offence" (an "unless" once met; fork F-405-1)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

@ref s 405(1) (src:28000-28017)
GIVEN `the person is guilty of an offence under section 405(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 405(1) the highest penalty on conviction` MEANS
    IF `the person is guilty of an offence under section 405(1)`
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 10000, 24, TRUE, FALSE)   -- a fine not exceeding $10,000 or imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or to both
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the penalty is that of a person guilty of the offence

@ref s 405(1) (src:28000-28017)
GIVEN `the name of the person` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 405 act`
`s 405(1) a person must not use a name ending in Limited or Berhad, or hold out incorporation, unless the business is incorporated` MEANS
    PARTY Individual `the name of the person`
    SHANT `s 405(1) use a name ending in the word Limited or Berhad, or hold out that the business is incorporated under this Act, when it is not`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Individual `the name of the person` BECAUSE "the person used a name ending in Limited or Berhad, or held out that the business is incorporated under this Act, when it was not"

-- (2): "A company must not use the word \"Private\" or \"Sendirian\" ... as part of its name if it does not fulfil the requirements required by this Act to be fulfilled by private companies".
-- Named as the bar. Whether the company fulfils those requirements is s 4(1) "private company"'s question, taken here as a fact.
-- src:28023 | (2) A company must not use the word “Private” or “Sendirian” or
-- src:28024 | any abbreviation thereof as part of its name if it does not fulfil the
-- src:28025 | requirements required by this Act to be fulfilled by private companies
-- src:28026 | and every corporation and every officer of a corporation who is in
-- src:28027 | default shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction
-- src:28028 | to a fine not exceeding $5,000 and also to a default penalty.
@ref s 405(2) (src:28023-28028)
GIVEN `the company uses the word "Private" or "Sendirian" or an abbreviation of it as part of its name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company fulfils the requirements required by this Act to be fulfilled by private companies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 405(2) the company is barred from using the word Private or Sendirian as part of its name` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company uses the word "Private" or "Sendirian" or an abbreviation of it as part of its name`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company must not use the word \"Private\" or \"Sendirian\" or any abbreviation thereof as part of its name"
    ELSE (IF `the company fulfils the requirements required by this Act to be fulfilled by private companies`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the bar is "if it does not fulfil the requirements"
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- "every corporation and every officer of a corporation who is in default shall be guilty": read as the corporation being guilty on the use, and the officer only if in default (fork F-405-2).
@ref s 405(2) (src:28023-28028)
GIVEN `the company uses the word "Private" or "Sendirian" or an abbreviation of it as part of its name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company fulfils the requirements required by this Act to be fulfilled by private companies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 405(2) the corporation is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the company uses the word "Private" or "Sendirian" or an abbreviation of it as part of its name` AND (NOT `the company fulfils the requirements required by this Act to be fulfilled by private companies`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "every corporation and every officer of a corporation who is in default shall be guilty of an offence" says nothing of a corporation for which an element fails; unmet element of an offence (split site type (i))

@ref s 405(2) (src:28023-28028)
GIVEN `the company uses the word "Private" or "Sendirian" or an abbreviation of it as part of its name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company fulfils the requirements required by this Act to be fulfilled by private companies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer is guilty of the offence knowingly and wilfully` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer knowingly and wilfully authorises or permits the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 405(2) the officer of the corporation is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF    `the company uses the word "Private" or "Sendirian" or an abbreviation of it as part of its name`
       AND (NOT `the company fulfils the requirements required by this Act to be fulfilled by private companies`)
       AND `s 408(3) the officer is an officer who is in default` `the officer is guilty of the offence knowingly and wilfully` `the officer knowingly and wilfully authorises or permits the commission of the offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "every officer of a corporation who is in default"; unmet element of an offence (split site type (i))

@ref s 405(2) (src:28023-28028)
GIVEN `the person is guilty of an offence under section 405(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 405(2) the highest penalty on conviction` MEANS
    IF `the person is guilty of an offence under section 405(2)`
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 5000, 0, FALSE, TRUE)   -- a fine not exceeding $5,000 and also a default penalty
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the penalty is that of a person guilty of the offence

@ref s 405(2) (src:28023-28028)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 405 act`
`s 405(2) a company must not use the word Private or Sendirian in its name unless it is a private company` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    SHANT `s 405(2) use the word Private or Sendirian in the name of a company that does not fulfil the requirements for private companies`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company used the word Private or Sendirian in its name without fulfilling the requirements for private companies"

-- src:28032 | (3) If a person carrying on a business, the person’s agent or a person
-- src:28033 | acting on the firstmentioned person’s behalf, in any way holds out
-- src:28034 | that the business is registered as a foreign company under this Act
-- src:28035 | when at the material time the business was not so registered, that
-- src:28036 | person shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction
-- src:28037 | to a fine not exceeding $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term not
-- src:28038 | exceeding 2 years or to both.
@ref s 405(3) (src:28032-28038)
GIVEN `the person carries on a business, is the agent of a person carrying on a business, or acts on the behalf of such a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person in any way holds out that the business is registered as a foreign company under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the material time the business was not so registered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 405(3) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF    `the person carries on a business, is the agent of a person carrying on a business, or acts on the behalf of such a person`
       AND `the person in any way holds out that the business is registered as a foreign company under this Act`
       AND `at the material time the business was not so registered`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "If a person carrying on a business, the person's agent or a person acting on the firstmentioned person's behalf, in any way holds out ... when at the material time the business was not so registered, that person shall be guilty of an offence" says nothing of a person for whom an element fails; unmet element of an offence (split site type (i))

@ref s 405(3) (src:28032-28038)
GIVEN `the person is guilty of an offence under section 405(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 405(3) the highest penalty on conviction` MEANS
    IF `the person is guilty of an offence under section 405(3)`
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 10000, 24, TRUE, FALSE)   -- a fine not exceeding $10,000 or imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or to both
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the penalty is that of a person guilty of the offence

@ref s 405(3) (src:28032-28038)
GIVEN `the name of the person` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 405 act`
`s 405(3) a person must not hold out that a business is registered as a foreign company when it is not` MEANS
    PARTY Individual `the name of the person`
    SHANT `s 405(3) hold out that the business is registered as a foreign company when it is not`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Individual `the name of the person` BECAUSE "the person held out that the business is registered as a foreign company when it was not"

§ `Section 406: frauds by officers`

-- (c): "has concealed or removed any part of the property of the company since or within 2 months before the date of any unsatisfied judgment or order for payment of money
-- obtained against the company". "Since" is on or after the date; "within 2 months before" is sg-periods P6, from the corresponding date 2 months earlier to the day before.
-- src:28044 | 406. Every person who, while an officer of a company —
-- src:28046 | (a) has by deceitful or fraudulent or dishonest means or by
-- src:28047 | means of any other fraud induced any person to give credit
-- src:28048 | to the company;
-- src:28050 | (b) with intent to defraud creditors of the company, has made
-- src:28051 | or caused to be made any gift or transfer of or charge on, or
-- src:28052 | has caused or connived at the execution of any
-- src:28053 | enforcement order against, the property of the company; or
-- src:28057 | (c) with intent to defraud creditors of the company, has
-- src:28058 | concealed or removed any part of the property of the
-- src:28059 | company since or within 2 months before the date of any
-- src:28060 | unsatisfied judgment or order for payment of money
-- src:28061 | obtained against the company,
@ref s 406 (src:28044-28061)
GIVEN `the day the property was concealed or removed` IS A DATE
      `the date of the unsatisfied judgment or order for payment of money obtained against the company` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 406(c) the property was concealed or removed since or within 2 months before the date of the judgment or order` MEANS
    IF    `the day the property was concealed or removed` AT LEAST `the date of the unsatisfied judgment or order for payment of money obtained against the company`
       OR `period: the date is within a period before` `the day the property was concealed or removed` `the date of the unsatisfied judgment or order for payment of money obtained against the company` 2 Months
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "since or within 2 months before the date of any unsatisfied judgment or order" (a period the text fixes in its own words; periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))

-- src:28044 | 406. Every person who, while an officer of a company —
-- src:28046 | (a) has by deceitful or fraudulent or dishonest means or by
-- src:28047 | means of any other fraud induced any person to give credit
-- src:28048 | to the company;
-- src:28050 | (b) with intent to defraud creditors of the company, has made
-- src:28051 | or caused to be made any gift or transfer of or charge on, or
-- src:28052 | has caused or connived at the execution of any
-- src:28053 | enforcement order against, the property of the company; or
-- src:28057 | (c) with intent to defraud creditors of the company, has
-- src:28058 | concealed or removed any part of the property of the
-- src:28059 | company since or within 2 months before the date of any
-- src:28060 | unsatisfied judgment or order for payment of money
-- src:28061 | obtained against the company,
-- src:28066 | shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine
-- src:28067 | not exceeding $15,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:28068 | 3 years or to both.
@ref s 406 (src:28044-28068)
GIVEN position IS A `s 4(1) "officer" what the person is`
      `while an officer of the company, the person has by deceitful or fraudulent or dishonest means or by means of any other fraud induced any person to give credit to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `with intent to defraud creditors of the company, the person has made or caused to be made a gift or transfer of or charge on, or has caused or connived at the execution of an enforcement order against, the property of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `with intent to defraud creditors of the company, the person has concealed or removed a part of the property of the company since or within 2 months before the date of an unsatisfied judgment or order for payment of money obtained against the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 406 the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF    `s 4(1) "officer" the person is an officer of the corporation` position EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND (   `while an officer of the company, the person has by deceitful or fraudulent or dishonest means or by means of any other fraud induced any person to give credit to the company`
            OR `with intent to defraud creditors of the company, the person has made or caused to be made a gift or transfer of or charge on, or has caused or connived at the execution of an enforcement order against, the property of the company`
            OR `with intent to defraud creditors of the company, the person has concealed or removed a part of the property of the company since or within 2 months before the date of an unsatisfied judgment or order for payment of money obtained against the company`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "Every person who, while an officer of a company, (a) ...; (b) ...; or (c) ..., shall be guilty of an offence" says nothing of a person for whom no limb holds; unmet element of an offence (split site type (i))

@ref s 406 (src:28044-28068)
GIVEN `the person is guilty of an offence under section 406` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 406 the highest penalty on conviction` MEANS
    IF `the person is guilty of an offence under section 406`
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 15000, 36, TRUE, FALSE)   -- a fine not exceeding $15,000 or imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years or to both
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the penalty is that of a person guilty of the offence

@ref s 406 (src:28044-28068)
GIVEN `the name of the officer` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 406 act`
`s 406 an officer must not defraud the company's creditors or induce credit by fraud` MEANS
    PARTY Officer `the name of the officer`
    SHANT `s 406 while an officer of a company, defraud the company's creditors or induce credit by fraud`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Officer `the name of the officer` BECAUSE "the officer, while an officer of the company, induced credit by fraud or defrauded the company's creditors"
